309, 0.02358371950685978, -0.0204957015812397, 0.032847777009010315, 0.007562913931906223, 0.01881505362689495, 0.03317570686340332, -0.009339207783341408, -0.02869398146867752, 0.011081342585384846, -0.025961222127079964, -0.01373895164579153, -0.0015551113756373525, 0.034241486340761185, -0.0048506492748856544, 0.036209072917699814, 0.005701221060007811, 0.02209436520934105]], "input": ["# Cystic Fibrosis Nutritional Management Community\n\nThis community focuses on the nutritional management of patients with cystic fibrosis and related health conditions. Key entities include various nutritional assessment methods, medical professionals, and specific health conditions, all interconnected to improve patient outcomes through tailored dietary interventions.\n\n## Importance of Nutritional Assessment\n\nNutritional assessment is a vital process in managing the health of patients, particularly those with cystic fibrosis. It involves evaluating dietary intake, clinical status, and biochemical markers to ensure that patients receive the necessary nutrients for their condition. This comprehensive approach is essential for identifying nutritional deficiencies and implementing effective interventions. The relationship between nutritional assessment and anthropometric parameters highlights the need for accurate measurements to inform dietary decisions. [Data: Entities (2349, 3253); Relationships (4294, 9625)]\n\n## Role of M.D. Higón Ballester\n\nM.D. Higón Ballester is a prominent figure in the community, recognized for his contributions to nutritional care for patients with cystic fibrosis and inflammatory bowel disease. His association with La Fe Hospital Universitari i Politècnic underscores his influence in medical research and practice. His work, particularly in the context of nutritional management, is crucial for advancing knowledge and improving health outcomes for patients. [Data: Entities (2249); Relationships (7141, 9428)]\n\n## Resting Energy Expenditure in Patient Management\n\nThe concept of resting energy expenditure (Gasto Energético en Reposo) is critical for understanding the energy needs of patients, especially those with specific health conditions like cancer. Accurate calculations of resting energy expenditure are essential for tailoring nutritional interventions to meet individual patient needs, thereby enhancing treatment efficacy. This aspect is particularly relevant for oncological patients, where energy expenditure can significantly impact nutritional status and overall health. [Data: Entities (2353); Relationships (5943, 9634)]\n\n## Nutritional Interventions for Frail Elderly\n\nIntervención nutricional focuses on dietary strategies aimed at improving the nutritional status of frail elderly individuals. This is particularly important in combating issues like sarcopenia and frailty, which can severely affect the quality of life. The relationship between nutritional assessment and intervention highlights the need for a tailored approach to dietary management in this vulnerable population. [Data: Entities (12704); Relationships (9099)]\n\n## Anthropometric Parameters in Health Evaluation\n\nPARAMETROS ANTROPOMETRICOS are essential for assessing body composition and nutritional status, providing valuable insights into an individual's health. These measurements are integral to the nutritional assessment process, allowing healthcare providers to evaluate the effectiveness of dietary interventions and make necessary adjustments. The interplay between anthropometric parameters and nutritional evaluation is crucial for managing conditions like cystic fibrosis effectively. [Data: Entities (3253); Relationships (4294, 9625)]\n\n## Nutritional Management in Cystic Fibrosis\n\nNUTRICION EN FIBROSIS QUISTICA emphasizes the importance of maintaining adequate nutritional status to improve the disease course and quality of life for patients with cystic fibrosis. This aspect of care is critical, as proper nutrition can significantly influence health outcomes and overall well-being. The relationship between nutritional management and other health assessments underscores the need for a comprehensive approach to patient care. [Data: Entities (2347); Relationships (9615)]", "# Critical Care Nutrition and Thrombosis Management\n\nThis community encompasses key medical entities involved in the management of critically ill patients, particularly focusing on conditions such as Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (SDRA), nutritional support through artificial means, and the complications associated with thrombosis. The relationships among these entities highlight the importance of integrated care in intensive settings.\n\n## SDRA and its nutritional management\n\nSDRA, or Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome, is a severe condition that necessitates specialized nutritional support for recovery. The relationship between SDRA and artificial nutrition is crucial, as enteral nutrition can significantly improve patient outcomes. Nutritional management is critical for patients with SDRA to support recovery and improve outcomes [Data: Entities (2163, 2164); Relationships (2838, 9063)].\n\n## Role of artificial nutrition in critical care\n\nArtificial nutrition is vital for critically ill patients, particularly those with conditions like inflammatory bowel disease and COPD. It aims to enhance nutritional intake and assist in the remission of diseases, thereby improving overall health. The use of artificial nutrition is a common practice in the Intensive Care Unit (ICU) to ensure that patients receive adequate nutrients during their recovery [Data: Entities (2164); Relationships (6948, 9031, 9061)].\n\n## Thrombosis as a complication in critical care\n\nThrombosis is a significant concern for critically ill patients, especially those receiving central nutrition. The risk of thrombosis can complicate medical interventions and pose serious health risks. Understanding the relationship between thrombosis and 